# API keys for live e2e runs (`--auth keys`), as 1Password secret references: no key goes in here.
# Copy this file to e2e/keys.env (git ignores it) and point each line at your own item:
#   op://<vault>/<item>/<field>     (an API Credential item keeps its key in `credential`)
# Then run under `op run`, which resolves the references into the run's environment only:
#   op run --env-file e2e/keys.env -- .venv/bin/python -m e2e run --mode live --auth keys --cheap
# Codex, opencode and pi use the OpenAI key; Claude Code the Anthropic one. Each agent gets only its own.
KEEPMUM_OPENAI_API_KEY=op://Develop/KEEPMUM_OPENAI_API_KEY/credential
KEEPMUM_CLAUDE_API_KEY=op://Develop/KEEPMUM_CLAUDE_API_KEY/credential
